# Update JRebirth Site Documentation

Keep the Maven Site docs in sync with framework code.

## Location

All doc pages live under `org.jrebirth.af/src/site/markdown/doc/`.
Format: Markdown plus Velocity (`.md.vm`).

## Sync checklist (when code changes)

1. Identify which doc page covers the changed module or feature.
2. If no page exists, create one.
3. Update or add `MACRO{include}` snippets pointing to the changed source files.
4. Verify snippet selectors still match; method or class renames break `aj:` selectors.
5. Update prose to reflect new behavior, parameters, or annotations.
6. If a new module is added, also update `TocList.vm`, `site.xml`, and `jrebirth-book.xml`.

## Style rules

- write clear, direct prose; avoid filler.
- use `**bold**` for a class or annotation name on first mention.
- keep code snippets from real source via `MACRO{include}`, not hand-written.
- body content goes inside a `#[[ ]]#` block to prevent Velocity parsing.

For the page template, snippet selector syntax, new-page steps, and the module-to-page map, see `reference.md`.
